## Deck

::bg{location="deck" time="dusk"}
::music{action="start" mood="sad" volume="down"}
@narrator: Seawater leaves Ilo's lungs in one long, burning heave.
::auto{character="brann" anchor="left" action="fadeInUp"}
@brann{emotion="grim"}: Breathe, boy. You were down there four minutes. Nobody comes back from four minutes.
@ilo: The crown. I saw the crown on the throne.
@brann: Everyone who goes down sees the crown. Most of them stay with it.
::auto{character="sefa" anchor="right" action="fadeInUp"}
@sefa{emotion="surprised"}: He's warm, Brann. He's warm. The sea gave him back.
@brann{emotion="grim"}: Then the sea wants something from him. Get him dry, and get him fed.
@narrator: Somewhere below the keel, something very large turns over in its sleep.
